The MIT licence above covers this package's own source. It does not cover
vendor/, which holds an unmodified copy of the prebuilt Slang wasm compiler
redistributed from shader-slang's GitHub releases.

Slang is licensed Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception. Its licence notice is in
vendor/SLANG-LICENSE.txt, the full Apache 2.0 text is in
vendor/LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt, and the licence texts covering Slang's bundled
third-party components (glslang, lz4, miniz, spirv-headers, spirv-tools, LLVM)
are alongside it in vendor/LICENSES/.

The binary is redistributed as-is and unmodified. Upstream ships no NOTICE
file, so Apache 2.0 §4(d) does not apply.
